media: h713-hdmirx: the mode table is THDMI_ModeList, not THDMI_ModeDetect

0136h calls the firmware's timing table by the name of the module that
follows it. AP3f took the two apart (umbau/re-apps/T1-note.md): the records
are the data payload of the TFD module THDMI_ModeList, and the ASCII string
the finder walks back from - 22 bytes behind the end of the array - is the
NAME of the next module, THDMI_ModeDetect.

So the finder is right and stays exactly as it was: it searches for that
string because that is what sits behind the array, and H713_TSE_NAME keeps
its value. Only what the comments call the table changes, plus one word in
the refusal, which now says "marker" instead of "module" because that is
what is looked for.

Comment and one string, in the driver and in the dtsi's description of
allwinner,firmware-tse. No code. Both board DTBs compile byte-identical
before and after (dtc, 34280 and 34327 bytes).

Follow-up to 0136h, which stays byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -2126,7 +2126,7 @@
 	 *                    at probe and never written: U-Boot loads
 	 *                    database.TSE there, and the timing table the
 	 *                    display firmware locks on (the TFD module
-	 *                    THDMI_ModeDetect, 152 records) is inside it.
+	 *                    THDMI_ModeList, 152 records) is inside it.
 	 *                    Without it the driver matches a measured timing
 	 *                    against the kernel's preset list instead.
 	 *
diff -ruN a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun50i-h713-hdmirx/sun50i-h713-hdmirx.c
@@ -276,18 +276,25 @@ static const char * const h713_hdmirx_hdr_scheme[] = {
  * capture window at all (1600x900, 21.09.2026: INCAP kept the previous
  * geometry and the wall the console).
  *
- * It is not in display.bin. The firmware asks its TFD manager for the module
- * "THDMI_ModeDetect" and keeps pointers into the loaded database.TSE image
- * (Init_ModeListCtx 0x8b132e04); U-Boot loads that file into the TSE window of
- * the MIPS reservation, 1 MiB at ARM 0x4be41000, and leaves it there for the
- * boot. 152 records of 54 bytes, byte for byte the same in the HY310's and the
- * HY300 Pro's firmware (T1, 21.09.2026). The serialiser writes the module name
- * 22 bytes behind the end of the array, which is how the array is found: back
- * in record steps while the leading dword stays a signal id of the vendor's
- * E_SIGNAL_ID space, 0x0002xxxx. Records are packed and the array is aligned
- * to nothing, so every field is read unaligned.
+ * It is not in display.bin. The records are the data payload of the TFD module
+ * THDMI_ModeList, which the firmware asks its TFD manager for and keeps
+ * pointers into inside the loaded database.TSE image (Init_ModeListCtx
+ * 0x8b132e04); U-Boot loads that file into the TSE window of the MIPS
+ * reservation, 1 MiB at ARM 0x4be41000, and leaves it there for the boot.
+ * 152 records of 54 bytes, byte for byte the same in the HY310's and the
+ * HY300 Pro's firmware (T1, 21.09.2026). Records are packed and the array is
+ * aligned to nothing, so every field is read unaligned.
+ *
+ * How the array is found is a separate thing from what it is called, and the
+ * two were one name until AP3f took them apart (umbau/re-apps/T1-note.md):
+ * the ASCII string 22 bytes behind the END of the array is the name of the
+ * NEXT module, THDMI_ModeDetect, not of this one. The finder below walks back
+ * from that string in record steps while the leading dword stays a signal id
+ * of the vendor's E_SIGNAL_ID space, 0x0002xxxx - which is unaffected by the
+ * correction and stays exactly as it was.
  */
 #define H713_TSE_RECORD		54
+/* the marker BEHIND the array: the next module's name, see above */
 #define H713_TSE_NAME		"THDMI_ModeDetect"
 #define H713_TSE_NAME_GAP	22	/* name to the end of the array */
 #define H713_TSE_ID_LO		0x00020000
@@ -3171,7 +3178,7 @@ static void h713_hdmirx_tse_load(struct h713_hdmirx *rx)
 	}
 	data = map;
 
-	why = "no THDMI_ModeDetect module in the TSE window";
+	why = "no THDMI_ModeDetect marker in the TSE window";
 	if (h713_hdmirx_tse_find(data, win[1], &start, &count))
 		goto unmap;
 
